{3*}[Dynamic unconfoundedness] 
    The following m-separations are true:
    \begin{align*} 
        \textnormal{\bf not}~ N_{t+1}(\underline{g}_{k+1}) \mathrel{\mathrel{\adjustbox{valign=c}{\begin{tikzpicture} \draw[decorate,line width=0.5pt, decoration={zigzag,amplitude=0.8pt,segment length=1.3mm,pre=lineto,pre length=0.6mm,post=lineto,post length=0.5mm}, {Classical TikZ Rightarrow[length=1mm]}-{Classical TikZ Rightarrow[length=1mm]}] (0,0) -- (0.515, 0); \end{tikzpicture}}} \ast \mathrel{\adjustbox{valign=c}{\begin{tikzpicture} \draw[decorate,line width=0.5pt, decoration={zigzag,amplitude=0.8pt,segment length=1.3mm,pre=lineto,pre length=0.6mm,post=lineto,post length=0.5mm}, {Classical TikZ Rightarrow[length=1mm]}-{Classical TikZ Rightarrow[length=1mm]}] (0,0) -- (0.515, 0); \end{tikzpicture}}}} A_k \mid S_k
      ~\textnormal{\bf in}\,\mathscr{G}(\underline{g}_{k+1}), ~ k \leq t \leq T.
    \end{align*}

Assume that $R_t \subseteq S_t$ for $t \in [T]$. Under Assumptions
    1, 2,
    assump:no-confounding-b, 4,
    and 5, we have the following recursion for
    all $t \in [T+1]$:  

    \begin{equation}

      \begin{split}
        &\mathbb{P}(\underline{N}_{t}(\underline{g}_{t-1}) = \underline{n}_{t}, \underline{A}_{t}(\underline{g}_{t-1}) = \underline{a}_{t} \mid A_{t-1}(\underline{g}_{t-1}) = a_{t-1}, S_{t-1} = s_{t-1}) \\
        = &\mathbb{P}(\underline{N}_{t+1}(\underline{g}_t) = \underline{n}_{t+1}, \underline{A}_{t+1}(\underline{g}_t) = \underline{a}_{t+1} \mid A_{t}(\underline{g}_t) = a_t, S_t = s_t) g_t(a_t \mid s_t)\mathbb{P}(n_t \mid a_{t-1}, s_{t-1}),
      \end{split}
    \end{equation}
    in which we use the convention that $A_0$, $S_0$,
    $N_{T+2}$, $S_{T+1}$, $A_{T+1}$, $A_{T+2}$ are empty.
